name: Bug Report
description: Report a defect in the public web application or any open-source component.
title: "[bug] "
labels: ["bug"]
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Thanks for taking the time to report a bug. Reproducible reports get fixed fastest.
        For protocol design questions, please use **Protocol Design Proposal** or **Discussions** instead.

  - type: dropdown
    id: surface
    attributes:
      label: Where did you encounter this?
      options:
        - yeblock.com (web application)
        - Documentation in this repository
        - Other (please describe in the body)
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: summary
    attributes:
      label: Summary
      description: A one-paragraph description of the problem.
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: repro
    attributes:
      label: Steps to Reproduce
      description: Numbered steps. Include URLs, browser, and any state required.
      placeholder: |
        1. Go to ...
        2. Click ...
        3. Observe ...
    validations:
      required: true

  - type: textarea
    id: expected
    attributes:
      label: Expected Behavior

  - type: textarea
    id: actual
    attributes:
      label: Actual Behavior

  - type: input
    id: env
    attributes:
      label: Environment
      description: Browser, OS, device — anything relevant.
      placeholder: e.g. Chrome 138 on macOS 15.4

  - type: checkboxes
    id: terms
    attributes:
      label: Checks
      options:
        - label: I have searched existing issues for duplicates.
          required: true
        - label: I am not reporting a security vulnerability through this template (security reports should go to ye@yeblock.com — see SECURITY.md).
          required: true
